st/docs/agent-mode)\n- In agent mode, your prompt is sent to the Gemini API with a list of tools that are available. The Gemini API processes the prompt and returns results.\n\n### 5. **IntelliJ Support (July 31, 2025)**\n- **Source**: [DeviceBase](https://devicebase.net/en/google-gemini/updates/use-gemini-code-assist-agent-mode-in-intellij-preview/7cl)\n- The update for Google Gemini with version Gemini Code Assist 2.43.0 from 08/01/2025 brings agent mode support to IntelliJ as of July 31, 2025.\n\n### 6. **First Steps with Agent Mode**\n- **Source**: [Medium - Google Cloud](https://medium.com/google-cloud/first-steps-with-gemini-code-assist-agent-mode-8d467840e32d)\n- A guide on how to get started with agent mode in VS Code by toggling the Agent mode in the Gemini Code Assist panel.\n\n### 7. **YouTube Review**\n- **Source**: [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NqMf-38rA6U)\n- A video titled \"Gemini AGENT Mode: NEW FULLY FREE AI Coder By Google\" describing it as Google's new, fully free AI coding assistant built to rival tools like Cursor and GitHub Copilot.\n\n**Key Takeaway**: Agent Mode appears to be a major update to Gemini Code Assist that was released in July 2025, transforming it into a more capable AI pair programmer that can analyze entire codebases and implement features, eventually replacing the previous tools-based approach in October 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
